# ================= PREMIUM EMOJI PATCH (self-contained, appended after imports) =================
# Converts the emojis below into Telegram Premium custom emoji wherever they appear in any
# message/caption this bot sends, without touching any of the existing send/reply call sites.
#
# How it works:
#   - python-telegram-bot's Bot/Message/CallbackQuery send/edit methods are wrapped once, here.
#   - When a call uses parse_mode="Markdown" (the only parse_mode this bot uses), the text/caption
#     is parsed with a small legacy-Markdown parser (bold *él*, italic _x_, code `x`, ```pre```,
#     [text](url) links) into plain text + formatting entities — replicating exactly what Telegram's
#     server would have produced from that parse_mode, so bold/italic/links/etc. keep working exactly
#     as before.
#   - custom_emoji entities are then layered on top for every character in PREMIUM_EMOJI_MAP found in
#     the text (only emoji you supplied an ID for — the rest are left as normal unicode emoji).
#   - The message is then sent with entities=... / caption_entities=... instead of parse_mode, since
#     Telegram's API does not allow combining the two.
#   - If a message has NO parse_mode (plain text), we skip the markdown parsing step and just inject
#     the custom_emoji entities directly.
#
# Requirement: custom emoji entities only render for you if either (a) you purchased a Fragment
# username for this bot, or (b) the bot's owner account (the Telegram account that created the bot via
# BotFather) has an active Telegram Premium subscription — Telegram then allows the bot to send custom
# emoji in messages sent directly to private/group/supergroup chats. If neither is true, Telegram will
# reject these sends with a "CUSTOM_EMOJI_INVALID" style error.

import re as _pe_re
from telegram import MessageEntity as _PE_MessageEntity
from telegram import Bot as _PE_Bot
from telegram import Message as _PE_Message
from telegram import CallbackQuery as _PE_CallbackQuery

