# gzip snapshot AND uploads it (in two ~15MB/~5MB parts) — the heartbeat logs
# show RAM jumping ~55-70MB during that window (143MB -> ~200-213MB). On a
# constrained free-tier container, back-to-back backups every 3 and 5 minutes
# (so every ~15 min BOTH land close together) keep RAM elevated almost
# continuously and are the most likely trigger for the host's own hard
# memory/resource limit silently killing the process (SIGKILL — which is why
# there's never a Python traceback: SIGKILL can't be caught, see
# _install_crash_visibility_hooks). 20/30 min still gives frequent, safe
# backups (a worst case of losing ~20-30 min of activity if the process ever
# does die) while cutting the memory-spike frequency by ~7x. Change these two
# numbers directly if a different interval is wanted — nothing else in the
